course: dictionary
lesson: 5771
title: Lunge: a sudden forward move
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe action, and the sentence around them shows you what the action looks like. «A boy in Florida went close to a pond's edge; a bigger alligator lunged out of the water, and he only just jumped back in time.» The alligator came out of the water fast, and the boy only just got away. So lunged means moved forward suddenly and with force.
explain: «The shoebill waits almost without moving before it lunges to grab fish.» Look at the order of the action: first the bird is still, then it moves. That sudden change from still to fast is the lunge.
explain: Lunge can also be a noun, a thing rather than an action: «He made a lunge for the ball.» Here a lunge is the sudden forward movement itself. Check any meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If «moved forward suddenly» still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Lunge means to move forward suddenly and with force, often to grab or attack something.
fact: As a noun, a lunge is a sudden forward movement, as in «he made a lunge for the ball».
fact: Useful phrases are lunge at, lunge for, make a lunge and do lunges.
fact: «Alligators can lunge very fast over a short distance, in the water and on land.»
fact: In a small boat, keep low and sit still, because «small boats tip over easily if someone stands up or lunges to one side».
exercise: «The alligator lunged out of the water.» What does lunged mean? | Swam slowly in circles | Made a loud noise | Fell asleep in the sun | *Moved forward suddenly and with force
exercise: «He made a lunge for the ball.» In this sentence, what is a lunge? | A slow walk | *A sudden forward movement | A type of ball
exercise: In PE you may do lunges. What is a lunge exercise? | *Step one leg forward and bend both knees | Lie flat and lift both legs | Run round the field twice | Jump up and down with arms wide
test: The shoebill waits almost without moving before it «lunges to grab fish». Why does the lunge look sudden? | It is sleeping and then wakes up | It is walking slowly towards the fish | It is flying high in the sky | *It has been still, then moves quickly forward in one burst
test: Which phrase shows a movement aimed at something? | *Lunge at | Sit still | Fall over | Go to sleep
exam: Which sentence uses lunge as a noun? | *He made a lunge for the ball. | The shoebill lunges to grab fish. | Alligators can lunge very fast. | The alligator lunged out of the water.
